  "nodes": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "props": {
        "content": "agents2 is the private repo that builds Pi and the other agent tools on each Mac from one set of profiles. This week it moved from *Pi works* to *Pi runs a team*. Long sessions now summarise themselves cheaply and keep their memory. Named agent roles replace the built-in ones. Skills reach Cursor's cloud agents without being copied into every repo. Most of the remaining commits fixed things that had been silently failing."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "props": {
        "title": "1. Long sessions that remember",
        "description": "Compaction (summarising old conversation to free up space) now uses a cheap model. Memory is saved before anything is thrown away."
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "sequence-diagram",
          "props": {
            "caption": "Facts worth keeping are saved before the summary replaces the old messages, so nothing important is lost.",
            "participants": [
              {
                "id": "pi",
                "label": "Pi session",
                "kind": "service"
              },
              {
                "id": "mem",
                "label": "OptMem",
                "kind": "store"
              },
              {
                "id": "cm",
                "label": "compaction-model",
                "kind": "service"
              },
              {
                "id": "haiku",
                "label": "Haiku 5.5",
                "kind": "external"
              }
            ],
            "steps": [
              "note over pi: context reaches 70%",
              "pi -> mem : save durable facts first",
              "mem --> pi : saved in background",
              "pi -> cm : compact these messages",
              "cm -> cm : drop the memory wake message",
              "cm -> haiku : summarise, up to 24K tokens",
              "haiku --> cm : summary",
              "cm --> pi : replace old messages with summary",
              "--- next session ---",
              "mem --> pi : wake view with memories"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "grid",
          "props": {
            "columns": 3
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "card",
              "props": {
                "title": "Compaction model",
                "tone": "accent",
                "size": "sm"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "prose",
                  "props": {
                    "content": "Each profile picks the model in `pi.settings.compactionModel`. Personal uses Haiku 5.5. The summary limit was raised so Haiku stops falling back to Opus."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "props": {
                "title": "OptMem",
                "tone": "accent",
                "size": "sm"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "prose",
                  "props": {
                    "content": "Long-term memory is installed and on in both profiles. A single-line memory survives sessions, compactions and model changes."
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "card",
              "props": {
                "title": "Follow-up suggestions",
                "tone": "accent",
                "size": "sm"
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "prose",
                  "props": {
                    "content": "The profile now chooses the model that suggests your next message (`followUpModel`). Personal uses Haiku."
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "props": {
        "title": "2. A team of named agents",
        "description": "Pi's built-in agents are off. Seven roles live in the repo, and each profile decides which model runs which role."
